-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 20  Molten Front -- the 15 timed action lists round 24 never imported
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 16_ brought the CALL_TIMED_ACTIONLIST callers across but not the lists they
-- call. 19 rows have been pointing at action lists that exist in nelt_world and
-- nowhere on our side, so every scene they drive has been silently dead.
--
-- CORRECTION, verified on the live DB 2026-08-06 after 16_ was re-applied: the
-- Leyara finale list 5391200 was NEVER part of this gap. 16_ has always carried
-- it (and documents the 5391200 waypoint dead-end itself, at its own lines 301
-- and 575). It read as missing only because 16_ had not been fully applied when
-- this round's sweep ran. It is excluded here so ownership stays with 16_.
--
-- Note the core logs NOTHING for this class -- a CALL_TIMED_ACTIONLIST pointing
-- at a list that does not exist is not validated at load, it just silently does
-- nothing at runtime. The gap is only visible from the DB:
--
--   SELECT s.entryorguid, s.action_param1 FROM smart_scripts s
--    WHERE s.action_type = 80 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM smart_scripts a
--      WHERE a.entryorguid = s.action_param1 AND a.source_type = 9);
--
--   3653107 Smothervine          -> 5310700 / 5310701  the spellclick chain
--   3653112 Subterranean Magma Worm -> 5311200 (9)
--   3653234 Anren Shadowseeker   -> 5323400/01/02/03/04 (37 rows, 5 lists)
--   3654025 Elderlimb            -> 5402500 (4)
--   3654070 Tenaron Stormgrip    -> 5407000 (5)
--   3653163 Rope                 -> 5316300 (5)
--   3653354 Escape Winds         -> 5335400 (2)
--   3652705 / 3652990 Captured Hyjal Druid -> 5270500 / 5299000 (9)
--   3649413 Cenarius Event Camera -> 4941300 (1)
--
-- 77 rows in total, all verified present in nelt_world. The list ids are the
-- SOURCE entry x 100, which is this downport's established numbering and is
-- what the already-imported callers name -- so they are inserted unchanged, NOT
-- offset. (3610817 Duggan Wildhammer on map 751 also calls a missing list,
-- 1081700; it is Plaguelands content from a different source and is out of
-- scope here.)
--
-- PARAM SWEEP. The +3,600,000 clone scheme is not applied to action or target
-- params by any generic import, so every one is rewritten explicitly below.
-- This is the same defect family as 116_ (quest objectives), 144_ (TEXT_OVER)
-- and 14_ (KILLED_MONSTER / SUMMON_CREATURE):
--
--   * action 33 KILLED_MONSTER param1 53234 -> 3653234, or Anren's own quest
--     step grants credit for a creature that does not exist.
--   * target_type 19 (closest creature) param1 53366 -> 3653366 Leyara and
--     52669 -> 3652669 Matoclaw. Both clones exist.
--   * action 53 WP_START param2 is a waypoint path id and those stay RAW in
--     this import -- 16_ already imported Malfurion's path 53912 unoffset and
--     it resolves. The four paths these lists need (52990, 53234, 54025 and
--     5323400, 20 points total) were never imported at all; section 4 fixes it.
--   * The eight spells they cast are section 1, which MUST be applied first:
--     SmartAIMgr discards any row whose spell is unknown, so applying the lists
--     without the spells would import them and immediately throw most away.
--     Same ordering constraint 19_ had against 16_.
--
-- KNOWN AND DELIBERATELY NOT "FIXED": list 5391201 row 1 does WP_START on path
-- 5391200, which exists in NEITHER database. Path 5391201 does exist (11
-- points) but it belongs to the 54109/54110 escape run and is correctly
-- referenced by lists 5410900 and 5411001, so repointing Malfurion at it would
-- be wrong, not a fix. Nothing calls list 5391201 in nelt either -- it is dead
-- upstream data whose only effect is one skipped-row line at boot, same class
-- as WaypointPath 16256/17238. Left alone rather than invented.

-- ---- 1. the 8 spells the lists cast (PREREQUISITE -- apply before section 3)
-- 98244/98246/98248/108268/98233/98429/98506 downported from the real Cata
-- 4.3.4 client, 151279 rebuilt from nelt_world.spell_dbc + spelleffect_dbc the
-- way 123_ rebuilt 151099-151276 (it is a Neltharion invention with no client
-- row anywhere). Generated by tools/gen_hyjal_spell_downport_r26.py -- re-run
-- the generator rather than hand-editing.

DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (98244,98246,98248,108268,98233,98429,98506,151279);

